      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-49074",
      ":question/problem": "The table below gives the values of a continuous function $f(x)$ over the closed interval $[2, 8]$ with a regular step size. If the left Riemann sum approximation of the area under the curve $y = f(x)$ with $3$ subintervals defined by the given points has a value of $16$, then what must be the value of $k$?\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $3$ | $k$ | $12$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
